# Shade worker-only configuration. Copy to backend/.env.worker (never commit it).
#
# The worker opens the viewing keys merchants upload; the API only seals them (agents.md §5.3: the
# API tier cannot decrypt viewing keys). So the private half of the seal keypair lives here and in
# no file the API reads. The worker also needs everything in backend/.env (DATABASE_URL, the
# secrets, VIEWING_KEY_SEAL_PUBLIC_KEY, ...); this file only adds to it.
#
#   docker compose     the worker service loads backend/.env, then this file; api and migrate
#                      never load it (and get VIEWING_KEY_SEAL_PRIVATE_KEYS blanked). The file
#                      must exist: without hosted detection, copy it with the value left empty
#                      (and leave VIEWING_KEY_SEAL_PUBLIC_KEY empty in backend/.env).
#   docker run         docker run --no-healthcheck --env-file backend/.env \
#                        --env-file backend/.env.worker shade-backend node src/bin/worker.ts
#   outside Docker     put the variable in the worker process's environment only, e.g. from
#                      backend/: NODE_ENV=production node --env-file=.env --env-file=.env.worker
#                      src/bin/worker.ts
#
# Development needs no file: the dev server runs the worker inline with a generated keypair.

# Paste the VIEWING_KEY_SEAL_PRIVATE_KEYS line printed by
#   npm run -s keys:seal -w @shade/backend
# (its VIEWING_KEY_SEAL_PUBLIC_KEY line goes in backend/.env). Comma list of base64 X25519
# private keys, newest first: to rotate, put the new key first and keep the old ones while
# viewing keys sealed to them remain. One of them must match VIEWING_KEY_SEAL_PUBLIC_KEY.
# Anyone holding this value can open every uploaded viewing key.
VIEWING_KEY_SEAL_PRIVATE_KEYS=
